m style="font-weight: inherit; letter-spacing: inherit; text-align: inherit; text-transform: inherit; text-decoration: inherit;"><br>I appreciate James Arthur’s solution-oriented approach to seafood, which is a welcome angle from the fear-mongering we often hear in terms of health and climate problems. We talk about how choosing sustainable and clean seafood is one of many ways to vote with your dollar to impact our food system for the better.</em></p></span></div><div data-rid="ad1d0d6b-c4d7-491e-83a9-dc0b224f4b15" class="r-dt9b1z alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p><span>- Dr. Mark Hyman</span></p></span></div></div></div><div data-rid="f16b6ebb-9b4f-46d4-869c-6d1df9592790" data-alchemy-url-hashmark="ugc" tabindex="-1" id="ugc" data-alchemy-url-hashmark-ignore="true" class="r-1o09i8s"><div data-rid="24714f69-ae74-40f4-a655-9ff7bbfba034" class="r-1d40s16"><div data-rid="e6e24772-ab4f-469e-8086-dc766cafbdda" class="r-1i87qq4"><div data-rid="428fad6b-080c-4776-8fda-f636379df3f6" class="r-8lv762"><div data-rid="a9f53a3b-be96-42bf-8ec5-b5484914552a" class="r-18yj042">

